  "notes": "USAGE:\nThe particle に marks what is being endured: ～に{耐|た}える. Sense 1 (human endurance) and sense 2 (physical resistance) share this pattern but differ in subject — sense 1 typically has a person, sense 2 typically has a thing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {痛|いた}みに{耐|た}える: endure pain\n- {寒|さむ}さに{耐|た}える: endure the cold\n- {圧力|あつりょく}に{耐|た}える: withstand pressure\n- {地震|じしん}に{耐|た}える: withstand an earthquake\n- {耐|た}えがたい: unbearable, intolerable\n- {耐|た}え{忍|しの}ぶ: to endure patiently\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{耐|た}える emphasizes stoic endurance or physical resistance. {我慢|がまん}する (to put up with) is more colloquial and implies suppressing complaints or desires. {堪|こら}える is close in meaning but often emphasizes holding back emotions or tears.",
